{"id":"mahabharata-1-219","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":219,"title":"एकोनविंशत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 219 · Indra withdraws; Maya is spared","summary":{"en":"A voice from heaven tells Indra that Takshaka has escaped and that Krishna and Arjuna are Nara and Narayana, beyond defeat, and Indra withdraws. Agni consumes the forest for fifteen days, and only six survive: Ashvasena, the demon architect Maya, whom Arjuna spares, and four young shaarngaka birds.","kn":"ತಕ್ಷಕನು ತಪ್ಪಿಸಿಕೊಂಡಿದ್ದಾನೆ, ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣಾರ್ಜುನರು ಅಜೇಯ ನರನಾರಾಯಣರು ಎಂದು ಆಕಾಶವಾಣಿ ಇಂದ್ರನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತದೆ, ಇಂದ್ರನು ಹಿಂದೆ ಸರಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಹದಿನೈದು ದಿನ ಅಗ್ನಿ ಕಾಡನ್ನು ಭಕ್ಷಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅಶ್ವಸೇನ, ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಉಳಿಸಿದ ದಾನವಶಿಲ್ಪಿ ಮಯ ಮತ್ತು ನಾಲ್ಕು ಶಾರ್ಙ್ಗಕ ಪಕ್ಷಿಮರಿಗಳು ಎಂಬ ಆರು ಮಾತ್ರ ಉಳಿಯುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"आकाशवाणी इन्द्र से कहती है कि तक्षक बच निकला है और श्रीकृष्ण तथा अर्जुन अजेय नर-नारायण हैं, और इन्द्र लौट जाते हैं। पन्द्रह दिन अग्नि वन को भस्म करते हैं, और केवल छह बचते हैं: अश्वसेन, अर्जुन द्वारा बख्शा गया दानव-शिल्पी मय, और चार शार्ङ्गक पक्षी-शिशु।","te":"తక్షకుడు తప్పించుకున్నాడని, శ్రీకృష్ణార్జునులు అజేయులైన నరనారాయణులని ఆకాశవాణి ఇంద్రునికి చెబుతుంది, ఇంద్రుడు వెనుదిరుగుతాడు. పదిహేను రోజులు అగ్ని అడవిని భక్షిస్తాడు; అశ్వసేనుడు, అర్జునుడు విడిచిపెట్టిన దానవశిల్పి మయుడు, నాలుగు శార్ఙ్గక పక్షిపిల్లలు అనే ఆరు మాత్రమే మిగులుతాయి.","ta":"தக்ஷகன் தப்பிவிட்டான், ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணரும் அர்ஜுனனும் வெல்ல முடியாத நரநாராயணர்கள் என்று வானொலி இந்திரனிடம் சொல்ல, இந்திரன் விலகுகிறான். பதினைந்து நாள் அக்னி காட்டை விழுங்க, அஶ்வஸேனன், அர்ஜுனன் உயிருடன் விட்ட அசுரச் சிற்பி மயன், நான்கு ஶார்ங்கக் குஞ்சுகள் என ஆறு மட்டுமே பிழைக்கின்றன.","ml":"തക്ഷകൻ രക്ഷപ്പെട്ടുവെന്നും കൃഷ്ണനും അർജുനനും നര-നാരായണന്മാരാണെന്നും, അവരെ തോൽപ്പിക്കാനാവില്ലെന്നും ആകാശവാണി ഇന്ദ്രനെ അറിയിക്കുന്നു; ഇന്ദ്രൻ പിന്മാറുന്നു. പതിനഞ്ചു ദിവസം അഗ്നി വനം ദഹിപ്പിക്കുന്നു; ആറുപേർ മാത്രം രക്ഷപ്പെടുന്നു: അശ്വസേനൻ, രാക്ഷസശില്പിയായ മയൻ, അർജുനൻ മാപ്പുനൽകുന്നയാൾ, നാല് ഇളം ശാർംഗക പക്ഷികൾ."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.219; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"खाण्डवदाहपर्व","titleEn":"Khandavadaha Parva (Burning of the Khandava forest)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तथा शैलनिपातेन भीषिताः खाण्डवालयाः ।\nदानवा राक्षसा नागास्तरक्ष्वृक्षवनौकसः ।\nद्विपाः प्रभिन्नाः शार्दूलाः सिंहाः केसरिणस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Terrified by that falling mountain, the dwellers of Khandava, danavas, rakshasas, nagas, hyenas, bears and forest animals, rutting elephants, tigers and maned lions,"}},{"n":2,"text":"मृगाश्च महिषाश्चैव शतशः पक्षिणस्तथा ।\nसमुद्विग्ना विससृपुस्तथान्या भूतजातयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"deer and buffaloes, and birds by the hundred, and other kinds of creatures, scattered in alarm."}},{"n":3,"text":"तं दावं समुदीक्षन्तः कृष्णौ चाभ्युद्यतायुधौ ।\nउत्पातनादशब्देन संत्रासित इवाभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Looking at the blaze and at the two Krishnas with weapons raised, they seemed frightened by the sound of the roaring omens."}},{"n":4,"text":"स्वतेजोभास्वरं चक्रमुत्ससर्ज जनार्दनः ।\nतेन ता जातयः क्षुद्राः सदानवनिशाचराः ।\nनिकृत्ताः शतशः सर्वा निपेतुरनलं क्षणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Janardana hurled his discus, shining with its own brilliance; by it those lesser kinds of beings, with the danavas and night-prowlers, were cut down by hundreds and fell into the fire in an instant."}},{"n":5,"text":"अदृश्यन्राक्षसास्तत्र कृष्णचक्रविदारिताः ।\nवसारुधिरसंपृक्ताः संध्यायामिव तोयदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The rakshasas, torn apart by Krishna's discus and smeared with fat and blood, were seen like clouds at sunset."}},{"n":6,"text":"पिशाचान्पक्षिणो नागान्पशूंश्चापि सहस्रशः ।\nनिघ्नंश्चरति वार्ष्णेयः कालवत्तत्र भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vrishni, O Bharata, went about there like Time, killing pishachas, birds, nagas and animals by the thousand."}},{"n":7,"text":"क्षिप्तं क्षिप्तं हि तच्चक्रं कृष्णस्यामित्रघातिनः ।\nहत्वानेकानि सत्त्वानि पाणिमेति पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Each time Krishna, slayer of foes, hurled that discus, it killed many beings and returned again and again to his hand."}},{"n":8,"text":"तथा तु निघ्नतस्तस्य सर्वसत्त्वानि भारत ।\nबभूव रूपमत्युग्रं सर्वभूतात्मनस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he thus killed all creatures, O Bharata, the form of that soul of all beings became exceedingly terrible."}},{"n":9,"text":"समेतानां च देवानां दानवानां च सर्वशः ।\nविजेता नाभवत्कश्चित्कृष्णपाण्डवयोर्मृधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of the gods and danavas gathered there, none was victorious in the battle against Krishna and the Pandava."}},{"n":10,"text":"तयोर्बलात्परित्रातुं तं दावं तु यदा सुराः ।\nनाशक्नुवञ्शमयितुं तदाभूवन्पराङ्मुखाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the gods were unable, by force against those two, to save the forest or put out the fire, they turned away."}},{"n":11,"text":"शतक्रतुश्च संप्रेक्ष्य विमुखान्देवतागणान् ।\nबभूवावस्थितः प्रीतः प्रशंसन्कृष्णपाण्डवौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shatakratu, seeing the hosts of gods turn back, stayed there pleased, praising Krishna and the Pandava."}},{"n":12,"text":"निवृत्तेषु तु देवेषु वागुवाचाशरीरिणी ।\nशतक्रतुमभिप्रेक्ष्य महागम्भीरनिःस्वना ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the gods had withdrawn, a bodiless voice, of deep and great sound, spoke to Shatakratu:"}},{"n":13,"text":"न ते सखा संनिहितस्तक्षकः पन्नगोत्तमः ।\nदाहकाले खाण्डवस्य कुरुक्षेत्रं गतो ह्यसौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your friend Takshaka, best of serpents, is not here; he went to Kurukshetra at the time of the burning of Khandava."}},{"n":14,"text":"न च शक्यौ त्वया जेतुं युद्धेऽस्मिन्समवस्थितौ ।\nवासुदेवार्जुनौ शक्र निबोधेदं वचो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"And you cannot conquer these two standing in this battle, Indra; hear these words of mine: Vasudeva and Arjuna"}},{"n":15,"text":"नरनारायणौ देवौ तावेतौ विश्रुतौ दिवि ।\nभवानप्यभिजानाति यद्वीर्यौ यत्पराक्रमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"are the gods Nara and Narayana, famed in heaven; you too know their might and their valor."}},{"n":16,"text":"नैतौ शक्यौ दुराधर्षौ विजेतुमजितौ युधि ।\nअपि सर्वेषु लोकेषु पुराणावृषिसत्तमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"These two, unassailable and unconquered in battle, cannot be defeated; they are ancient, the best of sages in all the worlds."}},{"n":17,"text":"पूजनीयतमावेतावपि सर्वैः सुरासुरैः ।\nसयक्षरक्षोगन्धर्वनरकिंनरपन्नगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are to be revered above all, even by all the gods and asuras, yakshas, rakshasas, gandharvas, men, kinnaras and serpents."}},{"n":18,"text":"तस्मादितः सुरैः सार्धं गन्तुमर्हसि वासव ।\nदिष्टं चाप्यनुपश्यैतत्खाण्डवस्य विनाशनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore, Vasava, you ought to leave here with the gods; and look upon this destruction of Khandava as fated."}},{"n":19,"text":"इति वाचमभिश्रुत्य तथ्यमित्यमरेश्वरः ।\nकोपामर्षौ समुत्सृज्य संप्रतस्थे दिवं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that voice and taking it as true, the lord of the immortals put aside his anger and resentment and set out for heaven."}},{"n":20,"text":"तं प्रस्थितं महात्मानं समवेक्ष्य दिवौकसः ।\nत्वरिताः सहिता राजन्ननुजग्मुः शतक्रतुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that great-souled one depart, the dwellers in heaven hurriedly followed Shatakratu together."}},{"n":21,"text":"देवराजं तदा यान्तं सह देवैरुदीक्ष्य तु ।\nवासुदेवार्जुनौ वीरौ सिंहनादं विनेदतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the king of the gods go with the gods, the heroes Vasudeva and Arjuna uttered a lion's roar."}},{"n":22,"text":"देवराजे गते राजन्प्रहृष्टौ कृष्णपाण्डवौ ।\nनिर्विशङ्कं पुनर्दावं दाहयामासतुस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the king of the gods had gone, O king, Krishna and the Pandava, delighted, had the forest burned again without any fear."}},{"n":23,"text":"स मारुत इवाभ्राणि नाशयित्वार्जुनः सुरान् ।\nव्यधमच्छरसंपातैः प्राणिनः खाण्डवालयान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna scattered the gods like the wind scatters clouds, and with showers of arrows he destroyed the creatures that lived in Khandava."}},{"n":24,"text":"न च स्म किंचिच्छक्नोति भूतं निश्चरितुं ततः ।\nसंछिद्यमानमिषुभिरस्यता सव्यसाचिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"And none could get out, cut to pieces by the arrows of the left-handed archer as he shot."}},{"n":25,"text":"नाशकंस्तत्र भूतानि महान्त्यपि रणेऽर्जुनम् ।\nनिरीक्षितुममोघेषुं करिष्यन्ति कुतो रणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even great beings there could not so much as look at Arjuna in battle, whose arrows never miss; how could they fight?"}},{"n":26,"text":"शतेनैकं च विव्याध शतं चैकेन पत्रिणा ।\nव्यसवस्तेऽपतन्नग्नौ साक्षात्कालहता इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"With one arrow he pierced a hundred, and with a hundred one; lifeless they fell into the fire, as if struck down by Time itself."}},{"n":27,"text":"न चालभन्त ते शर्म रोधःसु विषमेषु च ।\nपितृदेवनिवासेषु संतापश्चाप्यजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"They found no shelter on the uneven banks, and in the abodes of the ancestors and the gods there arose torment too."}},{"n":28,"text":"भूतसंघसहस्राश्च दीनाश्चक्रुर्महास्वनम् ।\nरुरुवुर्वारणाश्चैव तथैव मृगपक्षिणः ।\nतेन शब्देन वित्रेसुर्गङ्गोदधिचरा झषाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thousands of throngs of creatures, miserable, set up a great cry; elephants trumpeted, and deer and birds cried out; at that noise the fish in the Ganga and the sea were afraid."}},{"n":29,"text":"न ह्यर्जुनं महाबाहुं नापि कृष्णं महाबलम् ।\nनिरीक्षितुं वै शक्नोति कश्चिद्योद्धुं कुतः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For no one can even look at the mighty-armed Arjuna or at mighty Krishna, let alone fight them."}},{"n":30,"text":"एकायनगता येऽपि निष्पतन्त्यत्र केचन ।\nराक्षसान्दानवान्नागाञ्जघ्ने चक्रेण तान्हरिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who made for the single path out and came forth anywhere were killed by Hari with his discus, rakshasas, danavas and nagas alike."}},{"n":31,"text":"ते विभिन्नशिरोदेहाश्चक्रवेगाद्गतासवः ।\nपेतुरास्ये महाकाया दीप्तस्य वसुरेतसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With heads and bodies split, lifeless from the speed of the discus, those huge bodies fell into the mouth of the blazing god of fire."}},{"n":32,"text":"स मांसरुधिरौघैश्च मेदौघैश्च समीरितः ।\nउपर्याकाशगो वह्निर्विधूमः समदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fed by streams of flesh, blood and fat, the fire seemed to rise smokeless up into the sky."}},{"n":33,"text":"दीप्ताक्षो दीप्तजिह्वश्च दीप्तव्यात्तमहाननः ।\nदीप्तोर्ध्वकेशः पिङ्गाक्षः पिबन्प्राणभृतां वसाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With blazing eyes and tongue, a blazing wide-open mouth, blazing hair standing up and tawny eyes, he drank the fat of living beings."}},{"n":34,"text":"तां स कृष्णार्जुनकृतां सुधां प्राप्य हुताशनः ।\nबभूव मुदितस्तृप्तः परां निर्वृतिमागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Getting that nectar produced by Krishna and Arjuna, Agni was delighted and satisfied, and attained supreme peace."}},{"n":35,"text":"अथासुरं मयं नाम तक्षकस्य निवेशनात् ।\nविप्रद्रवन्तं सहसा ददर्श मधुसूदनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Madhusudana suddenly saw the asura Maya fleeing from Takshaka's dwelling."}},{"n":36,"text":"तमग्निः प्रार्थयामास दिधक्षुर्वातसारथिः ।\nदेहवान्वै जटी भूत्वा नदंश्च जलदो यथा ।\nजिघांसुर्वासुदेवश्च चक्रमुद्यम्य विष्ठितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Agni, wishing to burn him, driven by the wind, took bodily form with matted hair and roared like a rain cloud; and Vasudeva, wanting to kill him, stood with his discus raised."}},{"n":37,"text":"स चक्रमुद्यतं दृष्ट्वा दिधक्षुं च हुताशनम् ।\nअभिधावार्जुनेत्येवं मयश्चुक्रोश भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the raised discus and the fire eager to burn him, Maya cried out, O Arjuna, run to me!"}},{"n":38,"text":"तस्य भीतस्वनं श्रुत्वा मा भैरिति धनंजयः ।\nप्रत्युवाच मयं पार्थो जीवयन्निव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his frightened cry, Dhananjaya answered, Do not be afraid, as if giving Maya life, O Bharata."}},{"n":39,"text":"तं पार्थेनाभये दत्ते नमुचेर्भ्रातरं मयम् ।\nन हन्तुमैच्छद्दाशार्हः पावको न ददाह च ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Partha had given Maya, brother of Namuchi, that assurance, the Dasharha no longer wished to kill him, and Agni did not burn him."}},{"n":40,"text":"तस्मिन्वने दह्यमाने षडग्निर्न ददाह च ।\nअश्वसेनं मयं चापि चतुरः शार्ङ्गकानिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that burning forest, six were not burned by the fire: Ashvasena, Maya, and four Sharngaka birds."}}]}]}